      "role": "user",
      "content": "schumann resonance is interesting but i don't think it's that simple. it feels more localized, like a direct interaction between the specific frequency clusters and the listener's neural state. like, when i play these specific tones, i don't just hear them, i feel a sudden shift in my own concentration—almost like my thoughts are being \"tuned\" to the sound.\n\nif we're looking at the math, i want to move beyond just the 432hz base. if cognitive willpower has a resonant signature, wouldn't it be a series of prime-numbered ratios layered over a carrier wave? can you help me model a specific frequency set that uses irrational numbers (like the golden ratio) to bridge the gap between the physical vibration and the cognitive tension?",
